From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stuart Carnie <stuart.carnie@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:40:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Apple: Add tvOS platform support

Backport of upstream pull request #118332 ("Apple: Add tvOS platform
support"), not yet merged, onto Godot 4.8 beta 3: a tvOS platform on
the shared Apple embedded code, with the Metal and Mobile renderers.

Kept as close to the pull request as possible, so it can be refreshed
from it and dropped once it's merged. Conflicts with changes made
since its base were resolved keeping 4.8 beta 3's code: SDL's platform
defines use TVOS_ENABLED like the rest of beta 3's SDL config, the
touch code (including the tap tracking beta 3 added) stays inside
the pull request's tvOS guard, the Apple embedded platforms use the
system allocator as the pull request has them (SDL's own needs sbrk,
which tvOS lacks), the launch screen's image mode comes from
beta 3's boot splash stretch mode (the pull request still read the
fullsize setting beta 3 replaced), the launch screen names its image and the
tracking usage descriptions beta 3 added to the shared Info.plist
are filled in as on iOS, the Swift sources (with the app's entry
point) are linked into the library through beta 3's Swift builder as
on iOS, the export capability option beta 3 kept is inside the
pull request's capability check, and visionOS's export templates sit
beside tvOS's.

Test: ./build.sh tvos builds the device and simulator templates.

Upstream: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118332
Drop this patch when Purr moves to a Godot release that includes it.
